	/**
	 * Emptiness of a form field, judged on the prepared form data (isDataFieldEmpty) with one addition
	 * available only here, where the DOM is at hand: a field the form renders as an expression area
	 * alone. An empty multiple entity selector prints one hidden input per selected value, so an empty
	 * one has no main control at all and the prepared data carries no key for it, while the control a
	 * write lands in (`fieldCode_text`) is rendered anyway - such a field is judged by that control.
	 * The DOM check bounds the addition to that shape: ajax.prepareForm also drops a control the form
	 * DOES render (disabled, unchecked checkbox, unselected radio, empty file input, multiple select
	 * with no selection), and every one of those keeps falling through to the strict criterion, which
	 * treats the field as NOT empty. A selector emptied with the cross leaves an empty hidden input
	 * behind, so its key is present and the strict criterion handles it as well.
	 *
	 * Callers looping over many fields can pass a pre-taken form snapshot (readFormData/snapshotValues)
	 * to avoid re-running ajax.prepareForm per field; omitting it keeps the original single-field behaviour.
	 */
